# Pool hygiene (design/data/skills.toml [registry], master plan §5), all with test bots (TtlBot*: no Voice announcement
# to everyone, but the personal Voice line and the history are the same). `ttl registry seen <p> <days>` fast-forwards a
# holder's last-seen; `ttl registry sweep` is the return-to-pool pass without refreshing online players first
# (the 5-minute cycle refreshes them, so a real holder who is online is never returned).
# Expect: P (Rare berserker + Common seeker) is 31 days "inactive": both records return to the pool at once
# (history `return`), P no longer holds either (the bot is online, so reconcile took them back immediately: look for
# "[ttl] registry: took tensura:berserker back from TtlBotPoolP" in the log), and Q, seen 29 days ago, keeps its seeker.
ttlbot spawn TtlBotPoolP
ttlbot spawn TtlBotPoolQ
@sleep 3
# Records a cut-off earlier run left on test bots would count against the caps below (staging 20/11 00:48).
ttl registry testclear
ttl grant TtlBotPoolP berserker
ttl grant TtlBotPoolP seeker
ttl grant TtlBotPoolQ seeker
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP berserker true
ttl registry expect has TtlBotPoolP berserker true
ttl registry expect keyed TtlBotPoolP
# Active holders are untouched by a sweep.
ttl registry sweep
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP berserker true
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolQ seeker true
# 29 days is still fine, 31 is not (inactive_days = 30).
ttl registry seen TtlBotPoolQ 29
ttl registry seen TtlBotPoolP 31
ttl registry sweep
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolQ seeker true
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP berserker false
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP seeker false
ttl registry expect has TtlBotPoolP berserker false
ttl registry expect has TtlBotPoolP seeker false
ttl registry expect pending TtlBotPoolP 0
ttl registry expect last TtlBotPoolP return seeker
ttl registry history berserker
# The slots are free again: Q can take the berserker the returned record gave up (unless others filled it).
ttl grant TtlBotPoolQ berserker
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolQ berserker true
ttl registry expect last TtlBotPoolQ grant berserker
# Offline: a skill returned while its holder is away stays on them until they log in. Simulated by granting the skill
# to P outside the registry again (Tensura), returning the record, and letting `reconcile` (= the login) settle it.
tensura edit ability grant TtlBotPoolP tensura:seeker
ttl reconcile TtlBotPoolP
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP seeker true
ttl registry seen TtlBotPoolP 40
ttl registry sweep
ttl registry expect holds TtlBotPoolP seeker false
ttl registry expect has TtlBotPoolP seeker false
ttl reset TtlBotPoolP
ttl reset TtlBotPoolQ
ttlbot remove TtlBotPoolP
ttlbot remove TtlBotPoolQ
